MID_SE_Die_Sar_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Die_Sar_C_001: This one's useful. This one's poison, though.
MID_SE_Die_Sar_C_002: Hi, Diego. What are you doing here?
MID_SE_Die_Sar_C_003: Where I go and what I do isn't your business.
MID_SE_Die_Sar_C_004: Wow, rude. Guess you don't need my help\nforaging, then.
MID_SE_Die_Sar_C_005: You shouldn't have asked if you already knew.
MID_SE_Die_Sar_C_006: My village was in a desert—hardly any plants grew\nthere. Here it's nice and green.
MID_SE_Die_Sar_C_007: This one's good, and so is this one. Oh! And this!\nWe won't need to worry about food anymore.
MID_SE_Die_Sar_C_008: Mm? Hey, wait a sec. That's glirmosa.
MID_SE_Die_Sar_C_009: Oh? What a strange name.
MID_SE_Die_Sar_C_010: Don't eat that stuff. It'll be three days and nights\nof agony.
MID_SE_Die_Sar_C_011: Is it poisonous or something? I guess it tingles a bit,\nbut it's delicious.
MID_SE_Die_Sar_C_012: You ate some? What kind of iron stomach do\nyou have?
MID_SE_Die_Sar_C_013: I figure I might share some with my friends, since it's\nso tasty.
MID_SE_Die_Sar_C_014: Damned amateurs. Listen, don't feed anyone the\nthings you pick here without asking me first.
MID_SE_Die_Sar_C_015: I know from my time as a Har Hali warrior what's\nsafe to eat and what's not.
MID_SE_Die_Sar_C_016: But aren't you from the temples? Except...you're a\nchild of Damascar...
MID_SE_Die_Sar_C_017: One thing led to another until Orchel took me in.\nI'm with the temple of Credna now because of her.
MID_SE_Die_Sar_C_018: But my past as a Har Hali will never change.
MID_SE_Die_Sar_C_019: So you're staying in a temple as one of the people\nof the forest?
MID_SE_Die_Sar_C_020: I've said enough. Throw away that plant, alright?\nSee you around.
MID_SE_Die_Sar_C_021: Wait! I'm one of the People of the White Egg. I am\nan ally to you. I'd like to know you better.
MID_SE_Die_Sar_C_022: Oh, you're from the forbidden land, huh? That would\nexplain your odd fighting style.
MID_SE_Die_Sar_C_023: Go talk to Orchel. I'm sure she'll want to hear all\nabout it.
MID_SE_Die_Sar_C_024: Hang on! You're the one I want to talk to!
MID_SE_Die_Sar_C_025: I don't think a child of Damascar would know how\nto read, come to think of it.
MID_SE_Die_Sar_C_026: If that's the case, I wonder how he can work at\na temple...
